    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Proponents of \"race realism\" often point to the Heritability Index (HI), which suggests that about 40-80% of differences in IQ scores can be attributed to genetic factors. They suggest that genetic variation, such as differences in the ETNs (Evolutionary Tobacco Smoke) genes or the DRD4 gene variant, may contribute to variations in cognitive abilities. Some proponents also cite the notion of \" mosaic evolution,\" which proposes that different human populations evolved in distinct environments, resulting in genetic adaptations that correlate with specific cognitive abilities, such as the \" East Asian cognitive advantage.\" However, these claims are often based on cherry-picked data, and the scientific community remains highly skeptical due to the lack of empirical evidence and flawed methodology.",
